Your AWS VPC just ran out of available IP addresses.
You cannot rebuild the VPC.
Traffic must continue.
What would you do?

First, we should quickly free unused IPs by deleting unused EC2s, ENIs, and old resources.Then  add a new CIDR block to the existing VPC (VPC CIDR expansion) and create new subnets from it, so we get more IP space without rebuilding the VPC.
If needed,  move or scale workloads into the new subnets and use load balancers to shift traffic gradually.
To avoid this later, plan proper CIDR sizing or use multiple CIDRs from the start.


